css34: RoundToNearest rounds for SourcePawn 2 plugins

sm_RoundToNearest has returned (int)val (truncation) since upstream 34dedcaab
(2016-06-22, "Remove half-up rounding"). SourcePawn 1 plugins never reach the
native: the legacy runtime inlines RoundToNearest as OP_RND_TO_NEAREST, which
rounds in the current FPU mode (half to even). Plugins compiled by spcomp 1.13
(SourcePawn 2) call the native and get 0.6 -> 0, 1.5 -> 1, -0.6 -> 0. The native
now uses rintf, so both kinds of plugin get 0.6 -> 1, 1.5 -> 2, 2.5 -> 2,
-0.5 -> 0. Upstream has the same code (master). Issue #211.

diff --git a/core/logic/smn_float.cpp b/core/logic/smn_float.cpp
index de2c590f6c67296244dc2f56cdfa6047e7808ffc..d591e52f1474d4750fc79397fc8f19213da678a2 100644
--- a/core/logic/smn_float.cpp
+++ b/core/logic/smn_float.cpp
@@ -191,7 +191,9 @@ static cell_t sm_RoundToNearest(IPluginContext *pCtx, const cell_t *params)
 {
 	float val = sp_ctof(params[1]);
 
-	return (int)val;
+	/* css34: SourcePawn 2 plugins call this native; SourcePawn 1 plugins get OP_RND_TO_NEAREST
+	 * (current FPU mode, half to even) instead. rintf gives both the same result. */
+	return (int)rintf(val);
 }
 
 static cell_t sm_RoundToFloor(IPluginContext *pCtx, const cell_t *params)
